# docshell/test/navigation/iframe.html: compact behavior record

Coverage: complete. Product tests were not run.

Source context: {"language":"HTML","runtime":"browser test document","role":"test","component":"docshell"}

## Whole-file declarations, data, registration and contextual obligations (unit-1)

During document parsing, the inline script removes the leading hash from window.location.hash and writes an iframe whose src is that remaining string. It performs raw HTML concatenation without escaping; callers provide controlled test URLs. test_reserved.html uses it to create a same-origin parent fixture around an off-origin navigation helper, tries four navigation mechanisms, waits for completion, then checks that the parent frame remains accessible. Replacing frames.innerHTML removes each old fixture; the test clears it at the end. The file defines no functions.


Evidence: [docshell/test/navigation/iframe.html:1-8](75f159cb-93c7-514e-a5e4-c14303e7e45e.md)

